'''Caesar Cypher, Version 0.1

This project implements a Caesar cipher, which creates a secret message by changing all the characters by one value, so "a" becomes "b", "b" becomes "c" and so on.  Thus "Hello" becomes "Ifmmp".

This version, however, is incomplete and does not yet work.

This project is part of the book "Creative programming with Strype".
Authors: Michael Kölling and Neil C.C. Brown'''
#(=> Section:Imports
#(=> Section:Definitions
def encode_one_character (character ) :
    '''Encode a single character using a step one Caesar cipher (that is: shift one character forward).'''
    #The 'ord' function turns a character into a number...
    code  = ord(character) 
    #letter characters have codes over 32; spaces and tabs have codes <= 32
    if code > 32  :
        #... and the 'chr' function changes a number back to a character
        result  = chr(code + 1) 
    else :
        # leave spaces and newlines untouched:
        result  = character 
    return result 
